bute via s.xxx.new_attribute = ...\n156 |     def __setattr__(self, key: str, value) -> None:\n157 |         # _cache is used by a decorator\n158 |         # We need to check both 1.) cls.__dict__ and 2.) getattr(self, key)\n159 |         # because\n160 |         # 1.) getattr is false for attributes that raise errors\n161 |         # 2.) cls.__dict__ doesn't traverse into base classes\n162 |         if getattr(self, \"__frozen\", False) and not (\n163 |             key == \"_cache\"\n164 |             or key in type(self).__dict__\n165 |             or getattr(self, key, None) is not None\n166 |         ):\n167 |             raise AttributeError(f\"You cannot add any new attribute '{key}'\")\n168 |         object.__setattr__(self, key, value)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/computation/pytables.py:PyTablesExpr.evaluate`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n616 | def evaluate(self):\n617 |         \"\"\"create and return the numexpr condition and filter\"\"\"\n618 |         try:\n619 |             self.condition = self.terms.prune(ConditionBinOp)\n620 |         except AttributeError as err:\n621 |             raise ValueError(\n622 |                 f\"cannot process expression [{self.expr}], [{self}] \"\n623 |                 \"is not a valid condition\"\n624 |             ) from err\n625 |         try:\n626 |             self.filter = self.terms.prune(FilterBinOp)\n627 |         except AttributeError as err:\n628 |             raise ValueError(\n629 |                 f\"cannot process expression [{self.expr}], [{self}] \"\n630 |                 \"is not a valid filter\"\n631 |             ) from err\n632 | \n633 |         return self.condition, self.filter\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"raise AttributeError\", \"raise AttributeError Invalid dtype\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:ArrowAccessor`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n36 | class ArrowAccess