buf):\n417 |                 mask[i] = valid if isinstance(obj, str) else invalid\n418 | \n419 |             # Convert the mask array to a Pandas \"buffer\" using\n420 |             # a NumPy array as the backing store\n421 |             buffer = PandasBuffer(mask)\n422 | \n423 |             # Define the dtype of the returned buffer\n424 |             dtype = (DtypeKind.BOOL, 8, ArrowCTypes.BOOL, Endianness.NATIVE)\n425 | \n426 |             return buffer, dtype\n427 | \n428 |         try:\n429 |             msg = f\"{_NO_VALIDITY_BUFFER[null]} so does not have a separate mask\"\n430 |         except KeyError as err:\n431 |             # TODO: implement for other bit/byte masks?\n432 |             raise NotImplementedError(\"See self.describe_null\") from err\n433 | \n434 |         raise NoBufferPresent(msg)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/datetimelike.py:DatetimeLikeArrayMixin._quantile`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1515 | def _quantile(\n1516 |         self,\n1517 |         qs: npt.NDArray[np.float64],\n1518 |         interpolation: str,\n1519 |     ) -> Self:\n1520 |         return super()._quantile(qs=qs, interpolation=interpolation)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"Invalid dtype\", \"raise AttributeError Invalid dtype\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/ops/invalid.py:invalid_comparison`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n26 | def invalid_comparison(\n27 |     left: ArrayLike,\n28 |     right: ArrayLike | Scalar,\n29 |     op: Callable[[Any, Any], bool],\n30 | ) -> npt.NDArray[np.bool_]:\n31 |     \"\"\"\n32 |     If a comparison has mismatched types and is not necessarily meaningful,\n33 |     follow python3 conventions by:\n34 | \n35 |         - returning all-False for equality\n36 |         - returning all-True for inequality\n37 |         - raising TypeError otherwise\n38 | \n39 |     Parameters\n40 |     ----------\n41 |     left : array-like\n42 |     right : 